\subsection{Case studies}\label{sec:cases}

All transcripts below are verbatim outputs of the released system on the ChatGPT-subscription backend (Codex CLI, model \nbenchCxModel) recorded by the benchmark harness; tool calls are shown with their arguments and timing. The only edit is that the package's internal name, which the model sometimes repeats from the tool descriptions, is replaced by the system name. The figures shown with the cases were produced by re-executing the recorded tool calls with the same arguments in the English interface setting; the tools are deterministic, so they are the figures the agent offered for download, with English labels.

\paragraph{From a batch sheet to a prediction} Figure~\ref{fig:caseP05} shows the most common laboratory input, a per-cubic-metre batch sheet. The agent derives the ratios the model needs ($w/b = 227/650 = 0.349$, $s/b = 2.0$, binder fractions 0.77/0.23, PCE 0.5\,\% of binder), calls \texttt{predict\_properties} once for both targets, and reports each prediction with its 80\,\% interval and the defaults it assumed (28~d, 50~mm cube, moist curing). The width of the shrinkage interval, more than a factor of two, is a property of the literature pool that the model is instructed to pass on rather than hide.

