\begin{agentbox}
I'll check the wall's buildability and layer cycle-time window using the physical model, including collapse, buckling, and open time.\par
\textbf{Not printable as an unsupported straight wall under the calculator's default assumptions. There is no feasible layer cycle-time window.}\par
\par
\par\smallskip\begin{adjustbox}{max width=\linewidth}\begin{tabular}{p{0.47\linewidth}p{0.47\linewidth}}
Check & Calculated result \\
Current cycle, including both filaments & 60 s/layer \\
Total printing time & 48 min \\
Minimum cycle for plastic stability, safety factor 1.5 & 160.5 s/layer \\
Maximum cycle allowed by open time & 75.0 s/layer \\
Feasible window & \textbf{None: minimum exceeds maximum} \\
\end{tabular}\end{adjustbox}\par\smallskip
\par
\textbf{Buckling governs:} the free-wall model estimates instability at approximately \textbf{212.5 mm}. Plastic collapse also prevents reaching the target; its estimated height limit without the safety factor is \textbf{423 mm}. Even without that factor, the plastic-stability minimum cycle is \textbf{86.2 s}, exceeding the open-time limit.\par
\par
Assumed defaults: \textbf{12.5 mm layer height}, \textbf{29.61 mm filament width}, approximately \textbf{59 mm total thickness}, density \textbf{2,100 kg/m\textasciicircum{}3}, \textbf{E/tau = 25}, immediate printing after mixing, and no dwell or travel overhead.\par
\par
To proceed:\par
\begin{itemize}[nosep,leftmargin=1.2em]
\item Add bracing, returns, or wall thickness to address buckling.
\item At the current \textbf{60 s} cycle, the plastic-stability calculation requires either initial static yield stress \textbf{>=7.82 kPa} with Athix unchanged, or \textbf{Athix >=2.68 Pa/s} with initial yield stress unchanged. These thresholds \textbf{do not resolve buckling}.
\item Accelerator, VMA, or lower w/b are possible material adjustments, subject to extrusion testing.
\end{itemize}
These are deterministic physical calculations, not prediction intervals. Confirm fresh stiffness, density, and stability experimentally.\par
\par
Files: Assessment, cycle plot, cycle CSV, literature analogues.\par
\par
\end{agentbox}
