Both models passed all applicable task checks under the final scoring rules, with \nbenchCxPassn{} of \nbenchCxN{} passes for \nbenchCxModel{} and \nbenchCsPassn{} of \nbenchCsN{} for \nbenchCsModel{}. These checks cover tool selection, input extraction, database answers and the specified refusal and memory behaviours. The reported results include fresh-session reruns after integration defects were corrected and wording rules were expanded after inspecting responses. They describe the final tested configuration and scoring rules.

Mean numeric fidelity was \nbenchCxFidelity{} for \nbenchCxModel{} and \nbenchCsFidelity{} for \nbenchCsModel{}. The corresponding chance-match values were \nbenchCxControl{} and \nbenchCsControl{}. Automatic matching left \nbenchCxNuntraced{} of \nbenchCxNnumbers{} reported numbers unmatched for the first model and \nbenchCsNuntraced{} of \nbenchCsNnumbers{} for the second. Manual inspection traced these to retrieved database values or calculations from retrieved component masses beyond the recorded response digest. No fabricated quantity was identified in that inspection.

Tool errors occurred \nbenchCxToolerrors{} times with \nbenchCxModel{} and \nbenchCsToolerrors{} times with \nbenchCsModel{}. All were corrected within the same turn. Errors included missing footprint inputs and rejected or malformed SQL queries. Median wall time was \nbenchCxWallmedian{}~s for \nbenchCxModel{} and \nbenchCsWallmedian{}~s for \nbenchCsModel{} (Figure~\ref{fig:bench}). Median tool-call counts were \nbenchCxCallsmedian{} and \nbenchCsCallsmedian{}, respectively.

